Why Is Demand Increasing?
Advanced-node semiconductor manufacturing: Increasing complexity in semiconductor fabrication and the use of advanced lithography processes are driving demand for reliable photomask protection. Pellicles help reduce the risk of particle contamination affecting patterned features and manufacturing yield.
EUV lithography development: The source identifies next-generation extreme ultraviolet (EUV) pellicles as an important technology direction. Improving membrane transmission, thermal stability, and defect control is becoming increasingly important as lithography requirements advance.
Continued display manufacturing: Pellicles also serve large-area photomasks used in flat-panel display manufacturing. Demand associated with LCD and OLED production extends the market beyond semiconductor applications.
Fab & Technology Pulse: EUV Performance and Mask Protection Define the Technology Race

Pellicle technology is evolving alongside the requirements of advanced lithography. A pellicle must protect a photomask from contamination while maintaining the optical performance needed for accurate pattern transfer. This creates a difficult engineering balance: membrane materials must deliver sufficient transmission, resist thermal stress, and control defects without compromising lithographic performance.

The source identifies EUV pellicles as a key development area, with progress centered on higher transmission, improved thermal stability, and lower defectivity. These requirements distinguish advanced pellicle development from conventional mask-protection applications. At the same time, flat-panel display manufacturing remains relevant because large-area masks used in LCD and OLED production also require protection. Suppliers therefore serve different technical environments, ranging from advanced semiconductor lithography to display manufacturing. For equipment manufacturers and semiconductor fabs, qualification, reliability, and consistency are important considerations when assessing pellicle solutions. The source identifies several established and specialist suppliers, but does not provide enough verified comparative figures in its summary to establish a precise market-share ranking.

